WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.590
Haven't put on my uniform in a while.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.670
It's Kona-chan.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.510
Kona-chan!

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.220
Good morning!

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.390
My...

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.390
Kagami-san.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:45.890
Tsukasa-san.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.060
A very good day to you.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.020
Why, Tsukasa-san...

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.230
Your ribbon is crooked.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:55.900
Thanks.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.900
Gonna hurl.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.240
What brought this on, Kona-chan?

00:01:59.240 --> 00:01:59.940
Yes.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.820
I have become hooked on Marimite.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.780
Marimite?

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.080
Are you a kid?!

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.290
Hey...

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.420
Don't start copying their costumes, too.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.130
Um...

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.500
Is that called cosplay?

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.630
I wouldn't go that far.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:19.670
You mean it, right?

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.800
I already do plenty of that at work.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.220
<i>Oh, yeah...</i>

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.430
<i>You work at one of those places...</i>

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.390
But if Kona-chan was a high-class lady...

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.110
<i>Feels so wrong that I can't even picture it.</i>

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.400
Baseball games have been going
over schedule too much recently.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.820
Why do the people watching new anime get shafted?

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.820
If you want to watch anime that badly...

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.990
...you could get cable or something.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.740
Aren't there specialized channels for that stuff?

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:51.870
If I could...

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.410
God knows I want to...

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.750
But the cable guys were all like...

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.420
You can't get cable...

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.090
Yuki-chan.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.120
Good morning.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.680
Good morning, Tsukasa-san.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:06.470
You look kinda down.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.970
Did something happen?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.430
Actually, I went to have my cavity taken care of.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.100
You went to the dentist.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.020
Impressive!

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:20.480
Why are there so many follow-up
trips after a visit to the dentist?

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.740
I totally know what you mean!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.160
And it isn't just one or two trips!

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.700
Miyuki-san.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.080
Good day.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.830
Konata-san.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:31.990
Good day.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.450
Have you been well?

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:35.620
Thank you for asking.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:36.580
I'm pleased to see you looking well.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.130
<i>Yuki-chan's so amazing.</i>

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.500
<i>She's talking the same way...</i>
I'm pleased to see you looking well.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.550
<i>...but it doesn't feel weird at all.</i>

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.800
<i>And she isn't even questioning
the way Kona-chan's talking.</i>

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.390
This is the first time I've seen
a person say "good day" in real life!

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.430
Really?

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.980
It appears to be a regularly used greeting...

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.150
...at the girls' school my friends go to.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.520
A real school for rich girls is something else.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:02.860
How refined.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.860
Kuroi...

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.650
...told me to collect summer homework for her.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.530
Excellent work, Sebastian.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.160
S-Seba—

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.540
Butlers must be named Sebastian, do you not agree?

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.910
You do get that impression.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.160
Tell us a funny story, Sebastian.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.040
<i>Ain't happening!</i>

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:17.960
Okay.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.580
Vacation just ended...

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.340
...but you ain't got no time to be mooching around.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.670
Start thinking about your future...

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.490
...and put effort into studying.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.050
By future, she means choosing a major?

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.600
I guess high school is only a temporary stopping point.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.430
But you probably haven't done
much thinking about the future, right?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:36.560
Why?

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.600
Don't insult me!

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.270
'Cause...

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:42.270
You chose liberal arts to be in the
same class with everyone else, right?

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.400
Tsu-Tsukasa!

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.230
You blabbed!

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.490
Ah, sorries.
You blabbed!

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.690
And you told her...

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.070
...o-of all people!

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:48.860
Come on...

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.950
You should have just been honest.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.330
You hate being lonely, don't you?

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.410
There, there.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:55.950
Shut up!

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:04.920
Hey!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.300
I'm back!

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.340
Cousin Yui...

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.340
For my summer homework...

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:16.180
I did as you told me and wrote down
random stuff when I didn't know the answer...

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.140
...and now I have to redo it all!

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:20.060
Save me!

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.810
O-Okay...

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:22.310
But...

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:26.190
If you get help from me,
you might have to redo it again...

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:26.980
...if you know what I mean...

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:27.820
She got out of it...

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.410
An extension on homework without
an extension on summer vacation...

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.830
Maybe I should borrow Kagami's notes.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:57.390
The sound of cicadas puts me to sleep.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:02.060
Huh?

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.200
I see...

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.320
The schedule's off because the
baseball game went over.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.450
I guess it can be useful sometimes.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.410
My recorder's off!

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:21.620
Huh?

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:23.330
Where are your glasses, Yuki-chan?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.250
Actually...

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.960
They broke this morning...

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.510
I forgot that I left them on the chair...

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:30.670
...and accidentally...

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:31.970
I'm terribly sorry...

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.720
...but could I borrow your notes for today later?

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.050
Sure.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.390
You still got the clumsy thing going.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.180
<i>Konata-san...</i>

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.890
<i>Your handwriting is a mystery to me.</i>

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.230
<i>Tsukasa-san...</i>

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:47.190
<i>Hang in there!</i>

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.740
They sure are useless.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.530
Here.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:53.150
Thank you so much.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:56.320
Good thing we have the same teacher.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:57.120
Um...

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.950
But please keep this a secret...

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:03.330
I don't wish to ruin their good intentions...

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.580
I'm starving!

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:07.750
Yuki-chan!

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.960
Let's have lunch!

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:10.840
Tsukasa-san.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:11.670
Konata-san.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.050
Thank you for letting me use your notes.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.340
Nah.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:17.350
No need to thank us.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:21.270
I never expected Yuki-chan to borrow my notes.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:21.770
Well...

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:22.850
It's not happening again.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:28.810
U-Um...

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.400
Is there something on my face?

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.360
In games, when a character who wears
glasses shows up at school without them...

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.490
...they suddenly become popular...

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.570
But I guess that doesn't happen in real life.

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.450
I-It really doesn't.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.790
Unfortunately.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.620
Don't chocolate cornets kinda look like drills?

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.170
D-Drills...

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:51.880
D-Didn't we discuss which side
of a chocolate cornet was the head?

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:53.880
Like how the thin end looked like the bottom.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.380
On second thought...

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.510
...the fat end looks more like the bottom.

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.260
Bottom?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.100
That's one big bottom...

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.430
And layers of stomach.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.560
When the lower half of your body gains weight...

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.480
...it becomes difficult to buy skirts and the like.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:10.610
That's right!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.230
If you use your waist measurements,
you can't get it over your hips.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.860
If it fits your hips perfectly,
it's loose around your waist.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:19.120
You have no choice but to buy one
that's too big for your waist...

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.700
...and when you walk around in it
your skirt starts spinning, doesn't it?

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:23.450
That's right!

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:26.080
A body with layers of stomach looks like a cornet...

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.370
If you turn it on the side...

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.670
...you can play it like a cornet.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.840
If you turn it again, you can...

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.000
...put it on your head like a cornet.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.090
Was that supposed to be funny?

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:38.930
Weren't you dieting to make up
for the added summer weight, Sis?

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.430
But my weight went down...

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.810
...without my waist or hips changing.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:45.180
No, Kagami.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:48.310
I can see the fruits of your diet.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.060
Really?

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:50.900
It's plain to see.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:57.530
They say that when you diet you lose
weight in the places you don't want to first.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.610
Okay already!

00:08:58.610 --> 00:08:59.860
Stop right there!

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.080
When reading literature...

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.790
...the trick is to keep the theme in mind...

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.330
...and understand what the author is trying to convey.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.750
<i>I get it...</i>

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:14.250
I heard that people with poor eyesight end up
with nasty expressions that scare other people...

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.760
...but I guess...

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.210
...it depends on the person.

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:18.510
Hey, you!

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.010
When you said it depends on the person...

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.550
...you glanced over at me, didn't you?!

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.600
I've heard that thinner eyes make you look prettier.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.680
It makes you look more mature.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:31.690
Hey.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:32.650
Stop that!

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.190
She's late!

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:37.280
Stupid Konata...

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.690
What's she doing?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.280
She's here!

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:41.570
Sorry!

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:42.450
I'm late.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.490
Way late!

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:46.330
Someone who's always complaining
about night games lasting too long...

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.040
...shouldn't be so loose with time!

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.120
Well, you know...

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.420
All the games have been going over schedule lately so...

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.170
I guess it infected me.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:54.960
Like it's contagious!

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:55.590
So?

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.920
Why were you late?

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:57.670
Overslept?

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:58.460
No way.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.220
I'm not a child.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.840
Then give me an adult reason for why you were late.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.260
Well...

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:09.810
There was still plenty of time
left when I finished getting ready...

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:10.850
So to kill time...

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.230
...I started playing games and couldn't stop...

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.270
You suck.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:15.360
You're worse than a child.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:16.860
Oh, yeah.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:21.400
There are a bunch of cultural festivals and
sporting events during second semester, right?

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:22.860
And we have tests soon.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:27.370
Kona-chan is really athletic so she can do well in sporting events.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.910
I don't like sporting events 'cause they make me tired.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:34.080
Pretty rare to see such an athletic sit-inside-all-day type.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:37.250
I wonder what our class will do for the cultural festival.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:40.050
There isn't anything I'd want to do.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.130
These things...

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.340
...can never be decided...

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:44.640
...unless someone wants to do something.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.260
And the person who brings up
the idea usually gets put in charge...

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:49.310
...so nobody's willing to talk.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.890
And you have to stay after school to prepare.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.810
You won't be able to watch evening anime.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.360
Knew you'd say that.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.860
It's my turn to cook dinner tonight.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.820
Have to stop by the store on the way home.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.080
What are you going to make?

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.790
Everyone's favorite chicken curry!

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.280
Everyone in our family loves chicken.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:16.040
Curry, huh?

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:16.960
Sounds good.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.130
I've heard that letting curry sit
overnight makes it taste better.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.880
It works well.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:27.010
Then I'll make some extra and bring it for lunch tomorrow.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.300
Since there'll be leftovers anyway.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:31.310
Yes.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.380
This is the Hiiragi residence.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:33.890
Tsukasa?

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.390
Kona-chan!

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.900
Why are you calling so early?

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.190
The curry...

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.190
Curry?

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.150
The curry I made yesterday...

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:44.190
I let it sit overnight and it's spoiled now.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:45.860
No way.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.820
Really.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:47.820
Why?

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:50.280
Curry usually doesn't go bad in one day.

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:51.370
Right?

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.040
Did you put in anything weird?

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:53.750
I didn't.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:54.790
But...

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.290
...there was mold in it this morning!

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.000
So?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.210
Another cornet today?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.040
They taste good so it's okay.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.670
If you say so...

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.880
Oh, yeah...

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.550
I just noticed...

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.680
...but the difference between when your lunches are...

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.010
...made properly...

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.850
...or made frugally...

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.060
...is really obvious.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:18.310
Ts-Tsukasa and I take turns making lunch...

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.070
I'm not good with housework...

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.400
It always ends up being simple!

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.570
So sorry it's frugal!

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:26.360
What?!

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.860
So you're the type of person...

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.120
...who can blow up pots when they cook?!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.870
Nobody in the world can do that.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:35.620
Yuki-chan's lunch looks wonderful again today.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.460
Not at all.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.920
Today's lunch is just leftovers from last night.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:43.500
<i>Dinner at Miyuki-san's place...</i>

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.130
<i>Is really fancy...</i>

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.800
<i>And these are just the leftovers.</i>

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.260
Um...

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:51.760
What's inside these fried eggs?

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:55.890
We had some eel leftover last night so I added it in.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.600
You don't usually see leftovers for eel.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.560
The only thing that's ever leftover
at our house is moldy curry.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:05.530
Your house isn't normal.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.900
Good morning.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.030
Yo!

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.490
Look! Look!

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.370
They bought me a cell phone!

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.370
Good for you.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.910
'Cause I did well on my practical exams for once.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:19.460
Give me your number.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.210
I'll give you mine.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.890
I wonder what my number was.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.310
Um...

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:39.940
Hold on a second!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:54.830
Um... Um...

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:55.580
Konata.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.090
You have a cell phone?

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.250
But I usually forget it at home.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.790
Since Dad's the only one who ever calls.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.540
Doesn't that defeat the purpose of having a cell phone?

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:06.300
You think?

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:07.320
Keroro!

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:08.920
Isn't it cute?

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.930
They bought it for me with the cell phone.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:13.090
Oh, yeah...

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:16.640
There was a girl in our class who
had a bunch of straps on her phone.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.060
They weighed it...

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.090
...and the straps alone were 800 grams.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.690
That much?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:23.900
That's heavy, man.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.110
Once she took the straps off...

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.020
...her stiff shoulders were cured.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:30.780
Sounds like making a phone call
would count as weight training.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:36.410
Isn't it exciting how you never know
when you'll get a call on your cell phone?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.280
Really?

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.830
I hope someone calls me soon!

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:43.120
There's no need to get so excited
over a cell phone nowadays.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.250
By the way, did you find your number yet?

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.420
Not yet!

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:49.710
In England...

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:53.930
...there was a large struggle between the
House of Lancaster and the House of York.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:58.430
The two houses fought wearing
red and white roses respectively.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.930
Thus, this war was known as the War of Roses.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:05.350
It lasted from 1455 to 1485.

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:06.400
This...

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.480
M-Mine?!

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.090
It's my phone!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.240
Somebody finally called me!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:20.990
Who's this?

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:21.830
Okay.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:22.750
Confiscated.

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.830
Pick it up in the faculty office after school.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.170
What a relief!

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.750
She gave it back!

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:32.930
But junk mail already?

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:37.320
Dad?

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:39.430
Still at school.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:42.720
I was talking with Konata and Miyuki
and lost track of time.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:44.180
It's okay.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:45.730
We'll be home soon.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:46.640
Bye.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:49.980
Just a little late and look what happens.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:53.610
Yes?

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:55.590
Dad?

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:57.910
I'm still at school.

00:15:57.910 --> 00:15:59.890
I'm with Kona-chan and everyone.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.540
You'd think he'd get the idea after calling one of us.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.620
Fathers are always worried about their daughters.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:14.550
We sure get a lot of junk mail these days.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:18.760
It's better to make your address hard to guess.

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:20.140
That's how I did it.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.720
It's hard to guess?

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.020
In what way?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.180
My e-mail address is in roman letters.

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.060
iluvgiriswithglasses.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:30.190
I wanted to go with maids or something...

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:33.320
But maids and shrine maidens are popular and easily...

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.530
Hold it right there!

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:35.240
We get it already...

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:38.240
...so don't talk so loudly around the general public.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.990
Your conversation is a bigger
problem than the junk mail!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:45.540
Good morning!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:46.910
Yo!

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:52.170
What's wrong, Tsukasa?

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:55.340
My cell phone...

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.380
She left it in her pocket...

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:01.010
It's gone to a better place, huh...

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.930
I wonder if they'll buy me another one...

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:09.980
This boy was safe.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:11.610
Tenacious little guy.

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:15.730
Then the e-mail last night...

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:20.410
The one that said Kagami wanted her notes back...

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.240
That was the last one you sent?

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.240
Yep.

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.920
Did you reply?

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:26.160
Um...

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.540
You never respond immediately
when you get an e-mail, do you?!

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:33.090
I don't reply to people I can talk to whenever I want.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:34.500
Reply to e-mails through e-mail.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:35.920
We see each other every day.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.880
What's the point?

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:39.550
You're going to lose your friends.

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:40.430
Oh, well.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:42.090
Wasn't that big a deal anyway.

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:43.220
Don't decide that on your own!

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:49.350
And she didn't return my notes.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:57.400
Tsukasa!

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:58.720
I'm coming in!

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:00.780
Sis.

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:03.410
Wh-What is it?

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:04.240
What's wrong?

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:08.200
This manga I borrowed from
Kona-chan moved me to tears.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.370
Good morning!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.120
Thanks for the manga, Kona-chan!

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:12.500
It was great!

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.460
Wasn't it so stupid and hilarious?

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:18.550
I-It moved me to tears!

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:21.340
I find it hard to believe
you're talking about the same manga.

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:22.010
Here.

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:23.680
If you cry, you're with Tsukasa.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:25.350
If you laugh, you're with me.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:26.600
I'm not gonna read it!

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.810
I don't want to be classified with either of you.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:31.690
But I wanna see how Sis reacts.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:35.610
Is it wrong to want to know more about your friends?

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:37.360
In that case...

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.030
Did Attack No. 1 make you cry or laugh?

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:40.070
Laugh.
Did Attack No. 1 make you cry or laugh?

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:41.400
Cry.
Laugh.

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.160
Then what's your favorite manga?

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.790
Sgt. Frog.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.490
<i>I can't tell if these two are similar or not...</i>

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:53.000
Why don't you join a manga club, Kona-chan?

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.460
Since you love manga.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.340
Well, I'd be willing to do it...

00:18:57.340 --> 00:18:59.670
And it'd be a good use of time...

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:01.420
Draw. Draw. Draw. Draw.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:04.110
D-Did you even try on this?!

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.600
Incidentally, Konata-san...

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.510
What is this a picture of?

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:09.640
This is Tsukasa.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:11.560
This was me!

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:12.890
This is Miyuki-san.

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.480
Well, I could really stretch
and say that you captured her spirit...

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.770
This is Kagami.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:19.400
So I can breathe fire.

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:20.690
My...

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:24.030
It fits Kagami-san's image so perfectly.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:24.990
What a frightening child.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.950
Cut that out already!

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.040
There's a new volume of FMP out.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.830
Right, I guess there's a release date coming up.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:34.790
I'm heading to Gamers.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:35.750
Wanna come along?

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.000
Sorry.

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.040
I'll just stop by a local bookstore today.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:40.130
I have some other stuff to take care of.

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:44.670
You're supposed to come
with me as a sign of our friendship!

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:45.720
What is it?

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.300
You sure are clingy today.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:50.390
Besides, you shouldn't be using words like friendship.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.350
Well, you know...

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:55.730
I wanted you to give me your
purchase points as a sign of our friendship.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:56.400
So that's your idea of friendship.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.980
You've waited so long for me!

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:08.700
<i>It's quiet...</i>

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:13.500
<i>Is she mad about how I mixed up the
ribbons on my pigtails with sunflowers?</i>

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:19.630
<i>Me?</i>

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.540
<i>To Akira-sama?</i>

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:21.330
<i>You sure?</i>

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:23.580
<i>Understood.</i>

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:27.630
Uh.

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.390
It started already...

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:31.260
<i>No choice!</i>

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.640
<i>Before they change the channel...</i>

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:33.140
Go—

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.430
Good lucky!

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:36.520
Just kidding!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:37.940
Just wanted to say it.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.860
W-Well, we're on another episode of Lucky Channel!

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.690
I'm Minoru Shiraishi!

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.030
Akira-sama's in a bad mood so...

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:51.530
You said your own name
before the name Akira Kogami.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:54.240
Do you not understand what natural order is?

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:55.750
No, that's...

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:02.540
Looks like those pigtails of yours have been
getting ridiculously popular in certain places.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:04.340
I-I wouldn't call it popular...

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.300
Don't be getting full of yourself!

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:07.800
I'm terribly sorry!

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:08.800
Besides...

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:14.140
People were expecting Project
Fashionable Akira to show me in pigtails, right?

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.060
So what's this?

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:16.870
It's just as you say!

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:19.850
I'll go with twin drills!

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:21.400
T-Twin drills?!

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.730
<i>Don't underestimate the Getter's speed.</i>

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:24.480
No. 2, huh?

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.940
The age of pigtails is over!

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.070
The new thing is twin drills!

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.820
Isn't that what Konata said?

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:33.200
Drills are like a man's romance.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:34.200
Is it now...

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:35.660
Well, everybody!

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.540
You can catch the rest of this on
the radio show and our home page!

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.040
L-Look forward to next time.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.580
Bye-bee!

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:45.090
Say...

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:45.590
Yes?

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:47.010
About those pigtails...

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.220
Ah, the ones I had?

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:49.880
The ones in the real life picture.

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:50.380
Yes?

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:51.590
You had sunflowers on, right?

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:52.470
I did.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:54.390
That looked awfully familiar...

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:55.430
You can't mean...

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:56.220
How many years ago was it?

00:21:56.220 --> 00:21:56.470
H-Hold on a sec!

00:21:56.470 --> 00:21:57.520
In one of my...

00:21:57.520 --> 00:21:58.730
Eew! Eew!

00:22:02.310 --> 00:22:03.860
I was so nervous.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:06.110
It was cute and wonderful.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:09.950
Isn't it so nerve-wracking when
you're singing your first song?

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:11.740
You wonder if your voice can be heard and stuff.

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:13.240
Miyuki's next, right?

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:16.030
Sing us something full of memories.

00:22:16.030 --> 00:22:17.160
Why?

00:22:17.660 --> 00:22:19.330
May I have the mic?

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:20.000
Here.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.060
Go for it!

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:24.790
Um, I'm not used to this kind of thing.

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:27.420
Please forgive me if it offends your ears.

00:22:27.420 --> 00:22:28.510
Don't worry.

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:29.590
Go for it!

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:34.840
Manly.

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:35.970
I get it.

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:38.220
This ties in to the other Miyuki.

00:22:47.570 --> 00:22:49.360
Even her singing is manly.

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:52.240
This is a new kind of turn-on.

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:54.530
You're so cool, Yuki-chan!

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:33.030
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:34.070
I'm Tsukasa.

00:23:34.070 --> 00:23:35.660
Er, I'm already out of time?!

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:35.700
Next time:
Er, I'm already out of time?!

00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:36.320
Next time:

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:38.070
Don't Need Me to Have a Blast.

00:23:38.070 --> 00:23:39.490
Look forward to next time!
